<title>BELGIUM: BELGIAN INTERBREW'S 1996 EARNINGS RISE.</title>
<headline>BELGIAN INTERBREW'S 1996 EARNINGS RISE.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fionancial year: 12-months to</p>
<p>December 31 1996 (comparative figures are for the 15 months to</p>
<p>December 31, 1995)</p>
<p>(in billion Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net (excludes minorities)	4.1  vs     3.46</p>
<p>    Cahsflow				    15.27 vs    14.16</p>
<p>    Operating revenue			 96.60 vs    81.40</p>
<p>    Shareholders' equity		    42.43 vs    38.82</p>
<p>    Investments				  6.05 vs     7.10</p>
<p>    Total sales(in million hectolitres) 32.86 vs    28.90</p>
<p>NOTE - Privately-owned Interbrew NV is Belgium's largest</p>
<p>brewer and a world leader in brewing and marketing beer.</p>
<p>Comparative figures included five-months of sales from John</p>
<p>Labatt Ltd, Canada's second-largest brewer which Interbrew</p>
<p>bought in July 1995.</p>
</text>
